From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 11:39:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] bfd: restore the section_htab guards removed by
 b3dcdde51b0

ld segfaults for aarch64-pc-cygwin in two places, both freeing a
section hash whose objalloc has already been released:

1. Every link.  Any -lfoo searches for a dynamic archive first; when
   libfoo.dll.a is absent bfd_fopen takes its error path:
      objalloc_free / bfd_hash_table_free / _bfd_delete_bfd
      / bfd_fopen("libgcc.dll.a", fd=-1) / gldaarch64pe_open_dynamic_archive
   _bfd_delete_bfd calls bfd_free_cached_info, which releases the
   objalloc, then frees section_htab from it.

2. Every --out-implib, i.e. every DLL build:
      objalloc_free / bfd_hash_table_free / bfd_make_readable
      / make_head / pep_dll_generate_implib / gldaarch64pe_finish
   bfd_make_readable calls the target's _bfd_free_cached_info and then
   the generic one, which frees section_htab a second time.

Upstream removed both guards in b3dcdde51b0 ("BFD: Remove null pointer
checks for 'bfd_hash_table_free' calls") because objalloc_free became a
no-op for NULL.  That is true for NULL but not for a pointer left
dangling by an earlier free, which is what both paths produce.

Our stage-1 gcc is --disable-shared so libgcc.dll.a never exists and
path 1 fires on every link; path 2 fires whenever a DLL is built, which
the runtime needs.  binutils 2.44 predates b3dcdde51b0 and links the
same inputs fine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bfd/opncls.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bfd/opncls.c b/bfd/opncls.c
index a8fa6ebbf17..7131a3c4ed4 100644
--- a/bfd/opncls.c
+++ b/bfd/opncls.c
@@ -150,8 +150,12 @@ _bfd_delete_bfd (bfd *abfd)
   if (abfd->memory && abfd->xvec)
     bfd_free_cached_info (abfd);
 
-  /* The target _bfd_free_cached_info may not have done anything..  */
-  bfd_hash_table_free (&abfd->section_htab);
+  /* The target _bfd_free_cached_info may not have done anything..
+     Guard the free: bfd_free_cached_info above may have released the
+     objalloc that section_htab.memory points into, leaving it dangling
+     rather than NULL, so objalloc_free's null check does not help.  */
+  if (abfd->section_htab.memory)
+    bfd_hash_table_free (&abfd->section_htab);
   if (abfd->memory)
     objalloc_free (abfd->memory);
 
@@ -185,7 +189,12 @@ DESCRIPTION
 bool
 _bfd_free_cached_info (bfd *abfd)
 {
-  bfd_hash_table_free (&abfd->section_htab);
+  /* The target's _bfd_free_cached_info may already have released the
+     objalloc that section_htab.memory points into, leaving it dangling
+     rather than NULL (bfd_make_readable calls both in sequence), so
+     objalloc_free's null check does not help here.  */
+  if (abfd->section_htab.memory)
+    bfd_hash_table_free (&abfd->section_htab);
 
   abfd->sections = NULL;
   abfd->section_last = NULL;
